namely|specifying-what-was-mentioned|ADVERB|Specifying what was mentioned|Used to state exactly which person or thing an earlier general expression refers to.|cụ thể là; đó là|We need two materials, namely wood and clear varnish.|Chúng tôi cần hai vật liệu, cụ thể là gỗ và véc-ni trong suốt.|Often follows a comma; introduces the specific items, rather than merely one example among others.|0
temporarily|for-a-limited-period|ADVERB|For a limited period|For a period that is expected to end rather than permanently.|tạm thời|The reading room is temporarily closed while the ceiling is repaired.|Phòng đọc tạm thời đóng cửa trong lúc sửa trần.|Modifies a verb or participle; temporarily unavailable. It does not specify exactly how long the period lasts.|0
wisdom|good-judgment-from-understanding|NOUN|Good judgment from understanding|The ability to make sound judgments using knowledge and experience.|sự khôn ngoan; sự từng trải|Her wisdom helped the group settle the disagreement calmly.|Sự từng trải của cô ấy giúp cả nhóm giải quyết bất đồng một cách bình tĩnh.|Uncountable; practical wisdom, the wisdom of doing something. Wise is the adjective.|0
downtown|central-city-area|NOUN|Central city area|The central part of a town or city, especially its business area.|khu trung tâm thành phố|The old downtown has narrow streets and several small theatres.|Khu trung tâm cũ của thành phố có những con phố hẹp và vài nhà hát nhỏ.|Especially North American; often uncountable. The downtown of a particular city can name its central district.|0
downtown|in-the-city-centre|ADJECTIVE|Located in the city centre|Situated in the central area of a town or city.|ở trung tâm thành phố|We booked a room in a downtown hotel near the station.|Chúng tôi đặt phòng ở một khách sạn tại trung tâm thành phố gần ga.|Before a noun: downtown shops, a downtown office. Especially North American.|1
downtown|to-or-in-the-centre|ADVERB|To or in the city centre|In or towards the central part of a town or city.|ở; đến trung tâm thành phố|She went downtown to collect the repaired violin.|Cô ấy đến trung tâm thành phố để lấy chiếc đàn violin đã sửa.|Go downtown or work downtown, without to or in in these constructions; especially North American.|2
highway|major-road|NOUN|Major road|An important road that connects places and carries substantial traffic.|đường lớn; quốc lộ|The highway links the farming towns to the coastal port.|Đường quốc lộ nối các thị trấn nông nghiệp với cảng ven biển.|Countable; a highway, a highway junction. The word does not always imply a controlled-access expressway.|0
